2. Non-commercial research means scholarly or scientific investigation that is not carried out for
   commercial advantage or monetary compensation, by individuals or by universities, research institutes
   and other non-profit organizations. Publishing the results (papers, theses, presentations) is part of
   such research.

   Non-profit teaching means teaching at schools, universities and other educational institutions, or by
   individual teachers, for which no fee is charged for the use of the Work itself and which is not part
   of a commercial course or product.

3. Not permitted without a separate written license from the Licensor:
   a. any commercial use, including use in or for a product or service that is sold, licensed, offered
