   b. use by or for a for-profit organization, including product research and development;
   c. use in commercial courses, textbooks, applications or other commercial educational products;
   d. selling, sublicensing or relicensing the Work or any part of it.
   To ask for a commercial or other license, contact the Licensor (see "Contact" in README.md).

4. Attribution. Any use, copy or publication based on the Work must cite it as shown in CITATION.cff
   and keep this license and the copyright notice.

5. Modified versions. If you share a modified version, mark it clearly as modified, state what you
   changed, and share it under this same license.

6. No warranty. The Work is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. It summarizes published
   studies and teaching observations; entries graded C or D are hypotheses that have not been tested.
